      "summary_sent_score": 0.13815921545028687
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "He has also sought a direction to the Police Authorities not to arrest him,\npursuant to the aforesaid F.I.R.\n3.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 687,
      "end": 798,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2568421959877014
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "Learned State Counsel as well as learned counsel for the complainant submit that, upon investigation, charge sheet has been filed against the petitioner, as Investigating Officer found sufficient evidence to proceed against the petitioner and petitioner has challenged the charge sheet by filing Criminal Misc. Application under Section 482 Cr.P.C., which is numbered as No.1157 of 2022, which is still pending.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 799,
      "end": 1210,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 482",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1128,
          "end": 1139
        },
        {
          "text": "Cr.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1140,
          "end": 1147
        },
        {
          "text": "No.1157 of 2022",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1170,
          "end": 1185
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.17499440908432007
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Thus, it is contended that writ petition has become infructuous.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 1211,
      "end": 1275,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3019832372665405
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "The said contention, however, cannot be accepted.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 1276,
      "end": 1325,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.19434309005737305
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "Mere filing of charge sheet will not render the writ petition infructuous.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 1326,
      "end": 1400,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5306436419487
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "4. Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of M/s Neeharika Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. Vs. State of Maharashtra & others, 2024:UHC:8396 reported in AIR 2021 SC 1918, have laid down parameters for exercise of power under Article 226 of Constitution, in such matters.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 1402,
      "end": 1659,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1413,
          "end": 1426
        },
        {
          "text": "M/s Neeharika Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. Vs. State of Maharashtra & others, 2024:UHC:8396 reported in AIR 2021 SC 1918",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1442,
          "end": 1558
        },
        {
          "text": "Article 226",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1614,
          "end": 1625
        },
        {
          "text": "Constitution",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1629,
          "end": 1641
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2758711874485016
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "5. The impugned F.I.R. is on record as Annexure No.1 to the writ petition.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 1661,
      "end": 1735,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.14733897149562836
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "Perusal of the F.I.R.\nreveals that ingredients of offences levelled against the petitioner are made out.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 1736,
      "end": 1840,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1814272254705429
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "WPCRL/280/2021 on 12 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18420528/\n1 6.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1841,
      "end": 1936,
      "entities": [
