    "facts": "Petitioner has sought quashing of F.I.R. No.16 of 2021, registered against him for offence punishable under Section 323, 420, 452, 504 & 506 I.P.C. in Police Station Nanakmatta, District Udham Singh Nagar.\n",
    "arguments": "Thus, it is contended that writ petition has become infructuous.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "Mere filing of charge sheet will not render the writ petition infructuous.\nWhile exercising power under Article 226 of the Constitution, this Court is not expected to embark upon an enquiry into, whether there is reliable evidence or not.\nIt is not a case where FIR does not, disclose any offence.\nNone of the parameters laid down by Hon'ble Supreme Court, for invoking power under Article 226 of the Constitution for quashing an FIR, are met in the present case.\n7. In such view of the matter, there is no scope for interference with the impugned FIR while exercising extraordinary power under Article 226 of the Constitution.\n",
    "decision": "8. Accordingly, the writ petition fails and is dismissed.\n"
